This patch exposes startVPN/stopVPN as package-accessible methods in the
tailscale-android fork so VpnBridge.java can call them directly.

Apply with:  cd tailscale-android && git apply ../tailscale.patch

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
diff --git a/android/src/main/java/com/tailscale/ipn/App.kt b/android/src/main/java/com/tailscale/ipn/App.kt
--- a/android/src/main/java/com/tailscale/ipn/App.kt
+++ b/android/src/main/java/com/tailscale/ipn/App.kt
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 package com.tailscale.ipn

 import android.app.Application
+import android.content.Context

 open class App : Application() {
     companion object {
@@ -10,6 +11,20 @@ open class App : Application() {
         fun get(): App = app
     }

+    // ── Exposed for Termux:Tailscale plugin ───────────────────────────────
+    /**
+     * Start the VPN. Safe to call from any context; will no-op if already running.
+     * The caller must ensure VpnService.prepare() returned null first.
+     */
+    fun startVPNFromPlugin() {
+        startVPN()
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Stop the VPN and clean up the tunnel.
+     */
+    fun stopVPNFromPlugin() {
+        stopVPN()
+    }
+    // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

     override fun onCreate() {
         super.onCreate()
         app = this
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NOTE: Once the AAR is built from this patched submodule, update VpnService.java:

    // Replace the TODO stubs with:
    import com.tailscale.ipn.App as TailscaleApp

    case ACTION_START:
        (applicationContext as TailscaleApp).startVPNFromPlugin()
        break;
    case ACTION_STOP:
        (applicationContext as TailscaleApp).stopVPNFromPlugin()
        break;
